**/conformetry-templates/**
# Conformetry example fixtures: a template file holds mustache where an
# identifier belongs, so it is not parseable as the language its extension
# names. Each example's own conformetry.config.ts is formatted normally.
**/packages/ic-suite/conformetry/conformetry-examples/examples/*/instances/**
**/packages/ic-suite/conformetry/conformetry-examples/examples/*/templates/**
# Emitted from the conformetry configuration; the emitter's output is
# authoritative, and reformatting it makes every conformetry command fail the
# drift check after a `format` run.
**/.conformetry/**
# Callidescope writes this report and then checks the file back against what a
# fresh run would produce, byte for byte. Reformatting it makes
# `callidescope-examples:callidescope` report it stale the moment `format` runs
# — the same failure mode as the emitted conformetry plugin above.
**/packages/ic-suite/callidescope/callidescope-examples/output/**
# The meander sweep writes its index and family pages here, gitignored and
# gigabytes at the default edge budget, and nothing in it is this formatter's
# to rewrite. `.prettierignore` excludes it for its own formatter.
**/applications/meanderaw/output/**
**/data/wikipedia
**/data/wiktionary
yarn.lock

# 🕸️ Every dependency graph codependix writes as JSON. It renders them with
# `JSON.stringify(…, 2)`, which puts one array element per line; oxfmt collapses
# a short array onto one. Reformatting one therefore makes the very next
# `codependix map --check` fail against what `codependix map --write` just wrote — the
# same conflict this file already resolves for `.conformetry/**`, and the same
# reason `configuration/eslint.config.ts` turns `jsonc/sort-array-values` off
# for exactly these files.
**/codependix-*graph.json
